            "Penalties called 'busche' for taking 0 or most points",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Try to win exactly one low-value trick to avoid zero points. Avoid winning high-value cards (Pita, Aces, last trick). If you have the Pita, plan carefully as it's worth 8 points.",
          intermediate: 'Track which suits opponents are void in. Use the restriction on leading coins early to your advantage. Count points taken by each player to predict who is at risk of most/least points.',
          advanced: "Manipulate trick distribution to ensure you take some but not most points. Force opponents to take the Pita or last trick. Coordinate indirectly with other players to 'cover' (coprire) and prevent someone from getting zero points.",
          tips: [
            'Taking exactly one low-point trick is ideal',
            "Avoid the Pita (Ace of Coins) - it's worth 8 points",
            'The last trick is worth 3 points - factor this into calculations',
            'If you have no points late in the hand, try to win any trick to avoid 1 busca penalty',
            'If leading and have many points, consider giving tricks to players who already have points',
            'Watch for opportunities to force the Pita on specific opponents',
