          deckDescription: 'One 40-card Italian or Milanese deck used for reverse trick-taking: four suits with ten ranks each, all cards dealt out to four players. No jokers are used; the deck supports Ciapanò-style scoring where card points in tricks become penalties.',
          suitDescription: 'Four suits, either traditional Italian (swords, batons, cups, coins) or the French suits used in the Milanese pattern (spades, clubs, hearts, diamonds). There is no trump suit; players must follow the led suit when able, and coins have extra restrictions in the first trick.',
          rankDescription: 'Ten ranks per suit in Ciapanò order: 3 (highest), 2, Ace, King, Horse or Queen, Jack, 7, 6, 5, 4 (lowest). In the Busca scoring variant, threes, twos and picture cards are worth 1 point, aces are worth 3 points, and the Ace of Coins (Pita) is worth 8 points.',
